{"turn":3,"db":"agents/main/agent/openclaw-agent.sqlite","session_id":"18a2afda-e26b-40be-b17e-a8c491c6995c","seq":136,"created_at":1795318143876,"event":{"type":"message","id":"35739c61-dbb1-4cbb-af93-2efddcdb7e8e","parentId":"87068457-90ef-495a-8b59-46fb445b9bab","timestamp":"2026-11-22T03:29:03.876Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b5aaa8581a474e8ba6bfa9625e2d2e1d|fc_02934c855ec4ef3d016b02617e78d487d29f163dc9fd9245f0","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"gbrain serve: Run the MCP server: stdio by default, or OAuth 2.1 HTTP with --http. On a thin client, bare serve is a stdio bridge to the remote brain and takes only --surface, --advertise and --source-guard.\n\nUsage: gbrain serve [--surface verbs|starter|full] [--advertise verbs|starter|full] [--access full|read-only] [--source-guard] [--stdio-idle-timeout <s>] [--stdio-member <id>] [--fail-fast] [--cli-socket]\n       gbrain serve --http [--port <n>] [--bind <host>] [--public-url <url>] [--token-ttl <s>] [--enable-dcr] [--surface …] [--advertise …]\n\nFlags:\n  --http                      boolean  Serve over HTTP with OAuth 2.1, the admin dashboard and per-token scopes.\n  --surface <choice>          enum     Tool surface: the 7 memory verbs, the daily-driver ops, or every operation. stdio: env GBRAIN_SURFACE > --surface > config mcp_surface > full; --http ignores GBRAIN_SURFACE. One of: verbs|starter|full.\n  --advertise <choice>        enum     The tools tools/list shows, narrower than --surface; every tool --surface allows stays callable and request_tools (always listed) describes the rest. Overrides config mcp.advertised_surface. New stdio registrations from gbrain setup and gbrain bootstrap hooks pass --advertise verbs. One of: verbs|starter|full.\n  --access <choice>           enum     stdio only: read-only exposes read-scoped, non-mutating operations. One of: full|read-only.\n  --source-guard              boolean  stdio only: refuse writes unless the source binding is deliberate or unambiguous.\n  --stdio-idle-timeout <n>    number   stdio only: exit after this many idle seconds (0 = never).\n  --stdio-member <value>      string   stdio only: answer as this enabled access member (written into one harness entry by gbrain setup claude-code|codex --stdio-member <id>). Wins over config mcp.stdio_member; a disabled or unknown member reads as nobody. Refused where OpenClaw or Hermes is installed.\n  --fail-fast                 boolean  Exit non-zero with the classified error when the database is unreachable (no degraded mode).\n  --cli-socket                boolean  Postgres only, off by default (or config serve.cli_socket): answer this user's CLI search, query, get and recall over a private Unix socket in $GBRAIN_HOME/.gbrain/run/ instead of a cold connection per call.\n  --port <n>                  number   HTTP port (default 3131).\n  --bind <value>              string   HTTP interface to listen on (default 127.0.0.1; 0.0.0.0 for remote access).\n  --public-url <value>        string   The externally reachable base URL (OAuth issuer and redirect checks).\n  --token-ttl <n>             number   Access-token lifetime in seconds (default 3600).\n  --enable-dcr                boolean  Allow OAuth dynamic client registration (consent-bearing authorization_code clients).\n  --enable-dcr-insecure       boolean  Also allow consent-bypassing client_credentials DCR clients (implies --enable-dcr).\n  --log-full-params           boolean  Log raw request payloads instead of redacted summaries (debug only).\n  --suppress-bootstrap-token  boolean  Never print the admin bootstrap token (pair with GBRAIN_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN).\n  --print-admin-token         boolean  Print the generated admin token even when stdout is not a TTY.\n\nExamples:\n  gbrain serve\n  gbrain serve --surface starter --access read-only\n  gbrain serve --cli-socket\n  gbrain serve --http --port 3131 --public-url https://brain.example.com"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"exitSignal":null,"exitReason":"exit","durationMs":488,"aggregated":"gbrain serve: Run the MCP server: stdio by default, or OAuth 2.1 HTTP with --http. On a thin client, bare serve is a stdio bridge to the remote brain and takes only --surface, --advertise and --source-guard.\n\nUsage: gbrain serve [--surface verbs|starter|full] [--advertise verbs|starter|full] [--access full|read-only] [--source-guard] [--stdio-idle-timeout <s>] [--stdio-member <id>] [--fail-fast] [--cli-socket]\n       gbrain serve --http [--port <n>] [--bind <host>] [--public-url <url>] [--token-ttl <s>] [--enable-dcr] [--surface …] [--advertise …]\n\nFlags:\n  --http                      boolean  Serve over HTTP with OAuth 2.1, the admin dashboard and per-token scopes.\n  --surface <choice>          enum     Tool surface: the 7 memory verbs, the daily-driver ops, or every operation. stdio: env GBRAIN_SURFACE > --surface > config mcp_surface > full; --http ignores GBRAIN_SURFACE. One of: verbs|starter|full.\n  --advertise <choice>        enum     The tools tools/list shows, narrower than --surface; every tool --surface allows stays callable and request_tools (always listed) describes the rest. Overrides config mcp.advertised_surface. New stdio registrations from gbrain setup and gbrain bootstrap hooks pass --advertise verbs. One of: verbs|starter|full.\n  --access <choice>           enum     stdio only: read-only exposes read-scoped, non-mutating operations. One of: full|read-only.\n  --source-guard              boolean  stdio only: refuse writes unless the source binding is deliberate or unambiguous.\n  --stdio-idle-timeout <n>    number   stdio only: exit after this many idle seconds (0 = never).\n  --stdio-member <value>      string   stdio only: answer as this enabled access member (written into one harness entry by gbrain setup claude-code|codex --stdio-member <id>). Wins over config mcp.stdio_member; a disabled or unknown member reads as nobody. Refused where OpenClaw or Hermes is installed.\n  --fail-fast                 boolean  Exit non-zero with the classified error when the database is unreachable (no degraded mode).\n  --cli-socket                boolean  Postgres only, off by default (or config serve.cli_socket): answer this user's CLI search, query, get and recall over a private Unix socket in $GBRAIN_HOME/.gbrain/run/ instead of a cold connection per call.\n  --port <n>                  number   HTTP port (default 3131).\n  --bind <value>              string   HTTP interface to listen on (default 127.0.0.1; 0.0.0.0 for remote access).\n  --public-url <value>        string   The externally reachable base URL (OAuth issuer and redirect checks).\n  --token-ttl <n>             number   Access-token lifetime in seconds (default 3600).\n  --enable-dcr                boolean  Allow OAuth dynamic client registration (consent-bearing authorization_code clients).\n  --enable-dcr-insecure       boolean  Also allow consent-bypassing client_credentials DCR clients (implies --enable-dcr).\n  --log-full-params           boolean  Log raw request payloads instead of redacted summaries (debug only).\n  --suppress-bootstrap-token  boolean  Never print the admin bootstrap token (pair with GBRAIN_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN).\n  --print-admin-token         boolean  Print the generated admin token even when stdout is not a TTY.\n\nExamples:\n  gbrain serve\n  gbrain serve --surface starter --access read-only\n  gbrain serve --cli-socket\n  gbrain serve --http --port 3131 --public-url https://brain.example.com","noOutputTimedOut":false,"cwd":"/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1795318143869,"__openclaw":{"runId":"8449333a-28d4-4ae4-92b6-8111265cd1e7"}}}}
